            "review_title": "Review at THE SQUARE",
            "review_text": "Tiffany J\nHạ Long Bay, Vietnam5 contributions\n0\nDon’t bother\nJul 2020 • Couples\nLiving in Ha Long we came here for my partners birthday to treat ourselves. Unless you have a great sense of humour for the experience, don’t bother \n\nService was slow and poor, large crowds with children came in blaring “baby shark”, food came out so slowly that instead of dining together we had our mains one after the other. The 4* hotel ambiance they attempt is completely destroyed by crowding people together mixing couples and individuals seeking a high quality meal, with large families having set dinner menus. The menu was not fully available. I ordered the oven roasted chicken stuffed with spinach and ricotta with potato gratin, on cherry tomato stew.... I got a chewy, dry, over cooked chicken breast topped with a thin layer of spinach and Swiss cheese... with pepper gravy and French fries..... \n\nUnless you’re looking for a pricey place to take the whole family where you don’t mind being surprised by what you order, I’d give The Square a solid miss.\nRead more\nWritten July 8, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-12",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
