            "review_title": "Review at THE SQUARE",
            "review_text": "hannostamm\nSiem Reap, Cambodia1028 contributions\n0\nAverage food and service\nJul 2017 • Solo\nThere is not much choice when it comes to Western food in Ha Long so I thought I'd give this a try.\n\nThe service got off to a rocky start, first I was brought the main menu, then the pasta menu, and finally the drinks menu. This set the trend, whilst staff were friendly, they were also very inattentive and getting another drink or even the bill proved to be a challenge.\n\nThe interior is typical chain hotel coffee shop style and it was quite noisy, with lots of Vietnamese kids screaming and running around.\n\nThe food was mediocre at best. I had the Calamari rings. OK, but I have had better in a pub. The salmon steak tasted OK but had the thickness of a postal stamp. Vegetables were way undercooked and cold and, as the plate was also cold, the fish also became cold immediately. The highlight were the mashed potatoes, some of the best I have had in a while.\n\nThe floor around my table was quite dirty and the table wobbly, one of my pet hates.\n\nI would go back given the lack of choices in Ha Long, otherwise I'd give it a berth.\n\nFor the quality, I considered the USD 40 I spent quite pricey.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 16, 2017",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-12",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
